{"profile":{"name":"Shelley Carroll","ward":"Ward 17, Don Valley North","bio":"Shelley Carroll was first elected to Toronto City Council in 2003, representing Ward 33 Don Valley East; she had previously served as a Toronto District School Board trustee from 2000 to 2003. She resigned from council in April 2018 to run as the Ontario Liberal candidate in the Don Valley North provincial election, then returned to council after winning the newly formed Ward 17 in the 2018 municipal election, and was re-elected in 2022. She served as Chair of the Budget Committee under both Mayor John Tory and Mayor Olivia Chow, and became Chair of the Toronto Police Services Board in January 2025.","committees":["Budget Committee (Chair)","Executive Committee","North York Community Council","Toronto Police Services Board (Chair)"],"contact":{"email":"councillor_carroll@toronto.ca","phone":"416-338-2650"},"promises":[{"text":"Open a constituency office located within Ward 17, Don Valley North, so residents can meet their councillor in person within the ward rather than at a civic centre.","source":"https://www.shelleycarroll.ca/post/our-new-constituency-office-should-we-stay-or-should-we-go"},{"text":"Continue working with the community to build a Don Valley North that is \"liveable and affordable for generations to come.\"","source":"https://www.shelleycarroll.ca/meet-shelley"}]},"lobbying":{"total":1218,"term":342,"first":"2010-07-13","last":"2026-10-08","lobbyists":285,"clients":241,"subjects":540,"methods":{"Meetings":441,"Emails":539,"Phone calls":86,"Written":85,"Other or unreported":67},"top":[{"label":"Economic Development","count":294},{"label":"By-law / Regulation","count":271},{"label":"Licences / Licensing","count":192},{"label":"Planning and Development Application, Zoning By-law","count":151},{"label":"Planning and Development, Planning Policy / Study","count":88}],"years":[{"year":2010,"count":7},{"year":2011,"count":31},{"year":2012,"count":48},{"year":2013,"count":81},{"